---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Consulting" description="Senior expertise in backend and distributed systems for product teams: new products, persistent problems, architecture review.">
	<h1>Consulting</h1>
	<p>
		Radziszewski Software helps product teams design, build and stabilise backend and distributed systems. It is
		for teams that need senior expertise without adding headcount.
	</p>
	<p>
		Engagements are led by <a href="/about/">Rafał Radziszewski</a>, who brings over a decade of experience, mostly on new products and in early-stage teams.
	</p>

	<nav aria-label="Consulting">
		<a href="#services">Services</a>
		<a href="#expertise">Expertise</a>
		<a href="#references">References</a>
		<a href="#rate">Rate</a>
		<a href="#contact">Contact</a>
	</nav>

	<section id="services">
		<h2>Services</h2>
		<dl>
			<dt>New products</dt>
			<dd>Architecture and delivery of greenfield projects and MVPs, from first design to production, built to validate quickly and grow later.</dd>
			<dt>Persistent problems</dt>
			<dd>Diagnosis and resolution of recurring incidents, performance issues and reliability problems.</dd>
			<dt>Architecture review</dt>
			<dd>An independent assessment of a design or a running system, delivered as a written report with prioritised recommendations.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>

	<section id="expertise">
		<h2>Expertise</h2>
		<dl>
			<dt>High-reliability systems</dt>
			<dd>Healthcare authorization system that powered an entire application suite, handling millions of messages per day.</dd>
			<dt>Real-time systems</dt>
			<dd>Real-time messaging that delivered messages faster than the client could animate them.</dd>
			<dt>AI products</dt>
			<dd>LLM orchestration, long-term memory and post-processing pipelines for an AI coaching app.</dd>
			<dt>Data platforms</dt>
			<dd>Storage and data layer for a machine-learning training data platform.</dd>
			<dt>Blockchain integration</dt>
			<dd>Application mechanics integrated with on-chain systems.</dd>
			<dt>Algorithmic work</dt>
			<dd>Adapting and implementing algorithms for production, from Elo rating to k-means clustering.</dd>
			<dt>Performance tuning</dt>
			<dd>Finding and removing bottlenecks in production code, such as accidentally quadratic hot paths.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>

